// Every session host's latest AVD agent report in the last seven days, with a Problem column (1 or 0):
//   not Available and not Shutdown: the agent says something is wrong (a deallocated host is not unhealthy, spec section 5a);
//   Silent: not Shutdown, yet no report for two hours, so the agent or the VM stopped reporting.
// A host absent from the result never reported in seven days; an empty result means no agent reports at all
// (no hosts, or the diagnostic setting is gone), which the runbook treats as its own finding, never as clear.
// The two-hour silence threshold and the Shutdown status of a deallocated host are assumptions to confirm on the
// first sandbox run. Columns: learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-monitor/reference/tables/wvdagenthealthstatus
WVDAgentHealthStatus
| where TimeGenerated > ago(7d)
| summarize arg_max(TimeGenerated, *) by SessionHostName
| extend Silent = Status != "Shutdown" and TimeGenerated < ago(2h)
| extend Problem = iff(Silent or Status !in ("Available", "Shutdown"), 1, 0)
| project SessionHostName, Status, Silent, Problem, LastReport = TimeGenerated, LastHeartBeat, AgentVersion, SessionHostHealthCheckResult
| order by Problem desc, SessionHostName asc
